{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0013", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-equivalence-categories}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0a907c4b48865aa9684ffb9c047060758352e9802e73f8e6c5a19bff7e593f2a", "source_text": "A functor is an equivalence of categories if and only if it is both fully\nfaithful and essentially surjective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9c9390484bf7dfb4b10986978fa196d58b6634dc41291fc84f358850583a7bff", "unit_id": "tag:02C3:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0013", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F : \\mathcal{A} \\to \\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0002": "$F$", "MATH_0003": "$X \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{B})$", "MATH_0004": "$j(X)$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0006": "$i_X : X \\to F(j(X))$", "MATH_0007": "$F$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-construct-quasi-inverse}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:30309aed8e79b535f7f20f2f0ba0eff9b1c64ab77fed7288cee41effba3707f8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6d6e39b926e79839b351acf383cd68d16fa4cde8cf21d9b3e02b1fc6d8d25cf9", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be essentially surjective and fully\nfaithful. As by convention all categories are small and as <MATH_0002> is essentially\nsurjective we can, using the axiom of choice, choose for every\n<MATH_0003> an object <MATH_0004> of <MATH_0005> and an\nisomorphism <MATH_0006>. Then we apply\nLemma <REF_0001>\nusing that <MATH_0007> is fully faithful.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ef067009899d0f870cc1f1540f6c3b165a4082b01519d5a1813a666c2dd4b3f8", "unit_id": "tag:02C3:proof"}
